// The executable's own icon, as seen in Explorer, the taskbar and Alt-Tab.
//
// Separate from the notification-area icon, which WinBarPresenter draws at
// runtime, and separate again from the installer's, which the Inno script names
// directly. All three come from the same artwork; only this one has to travel
// inside the binary.
//
// The numeric id matters: Explorer shows the icon with the LOWEST id, so this
// stays 1 and nothing else in this file may claim a smaller one.
1 ICON "..\\..\\resources\\hyperwave.ico"
